okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Unknown error on sarah-ai: Claude Code exited with code 1 right after launch."
reported: "User, 2026-09-27: 'sarah-ai@100.64.0.63 사라 마신에서 알수 없는 에러' with the ciel diagnostic 'Claude Code exited with code 1 while routed through http://127.0.0.1:8804' and channel_stdin_proxy_blocked lines."
confirmed:
  screen: "tmux aap-agent-8: Claude Code 2.1.283 folder trust dialog for /home/sarah-ai ('Quick safety check', '❯ No, exit', 'Yes, I trust this folder', 'Enter to confirm · Esc to cancel'), then the exit diagnostic."
  trust_state: "~/.claude.json projects['/home/sarah-ai'].hasTrustDialogAccepted = False, numStartups 2: the dialog shows on every start."
  channel_backlog: "runtime-inputs 183..229 (Walkie com.ciel.walkie.support.message) queued at 20:23:11-13 local."
  timeline: "Launch 1 (router 8805): batch 183-190 written ~6.5 s after the messages arrived, recorded failed prompt_not_submitted. Launch 2 (router 8804, launch-state time 1790558692.97): batch 191-198 recorded failed prompt_not_submitted 4.43 s after launch; Claude exited with code 1."
  repro_on_host: "sarah-ai, temp untrusted dir, real claude under a python pty: trust dialog 1.1 s after start; writing text then Enter -> exit status 1."
  cause: "The POSIX channel relay injected prompts (text + Enter) with no check that the CLI was at its input screen; in the trust dialog the Enter selected the default 'No, exit'."
change:
  - "New ciel_runtime_support/terminal_modal_guard.TerminalModalGuard: strips ANSI and whitespace from the child's output and reports a dialog while the last dialog marker (claude.exe: Quick safety check, Yes, I trust this folder, Enter to confirm; codex.exe: Do you trust the contents of this directory?, Press enter to continue) is newer than the last input-screen marker (for shortcuts, to interrupt, shift+tab to cycle)."
  - "channel_terminal_proxy (POSIX): feeds every child output chunk to the guard and passes input_ready=not dialog to poll_pending_compaction / poll_pending_channel_messages; logs channel_stdin_proxy_input_held / _released."
verification:
  tests: "tests/test_terminal_modal_guard.py: 4 guard tests (real-shaped Claude trust screen with cursor-move spacing, 7-byte/5-byte split reads, Codex prompt, no false hold) + 1 real-PTY relay test with a Claude-like child that exits 1 on any key during its trust dialog. WSL: 5 OK. The relay test against the pre-fix relay (HEAD 1550aa7) FAILS with 'exit: No' / CHILD_EXIT=1 HELD=False, i.e. the sarah symptom."
  groups: "run_test_group unit 1656 OK (skipped 48), channel 434 OK (skipped 80), runtime 320 OK (skipped 19), router 1154 OK; ruff clean."
not_verified: "Windows ConPTY relay has no such guard yet (not changed)."
follow_up:
  gap: "Real claude on sarah-ai through the installed 5678c0d relay (temp untrusted dir, injection attempted at once): Claude stayed up 15 s and the relay logged input_held, but the injection attempt (t+0.20 s) came before the dialog was drawn (held at t+0.53 s): input written before the first screen was not guarded."
  change: "TerminalModalGuard also holds until the CLI's first input screen (a ready marker), for at most CIEL_RUNTIME_CHANNEL_STARTUP_HOLD_SECONDS (default 15 s) when no dialog is shown, so runtimes without these markers (agy, muse, ...) still get input. The synthetic-child PTY test sets the hold to 0."
  tests: "WSL tests.test_terminal_modal_guard + tests.test_pty_master_writer: 11 OK in 3.7 s. run_test_group unit 1657 OK (skipped 48), channel 434 OK (skipped 80), runtime 320 OK (skipped 19), router 1154 OK."
  self_update_check: "Installed code on robert-ai (f91af10) and sarah-ai (5678c0d): update check queries @nightly -> 0.2.51-nightly.20260924-003723.ae32250, would upgrade False (no downgrade on restart)."
deployment:
  commits: "5678c0d and 95c5cc6 pushed to origin/nightly. npm publish is still blocked (NPM_TOKEN), so the npm pack of 95c5cc6 (0.2.51-nightly.20260928-015034.95c5cc6) was installed by hand."
  sarah_ai: "Installed with no ciel-runtime running; 5678c0d kept in ~/.ciel-runtime-backup/. Real claude through the installed relay: input_held at +0.20 s, no injection for 20 s, Claude still running. Trust for /home/sarah-ai is still not accepted (the user has to pick 'Yes, I trust this folder'). Walkie backlog: 183..198 recorded failed prompt_not_submitted (not delivered), 199..229 queued, cursor last_id 182."
  robert_ai_cindy_ai: "User, 2026-09-27: '나머지도 파일을 모두 업데이트해줘. 나중에 재시작할게'. Both had `ciel_runtime.py cli --continue` and `serve` running, so the install script was run with FORCE=1 (files replaced under the running sessions; f91af10 kept in ~/.ciel-runtime-backup/). Import check and `ciel-runtime tokens --help` succeeded; the running pids were still alive afterwards. The running processes keep the old code until the user restarts them."
  self_update_check: "Installed code on robert-ai, cindy-ai and sarah-ai (95c5cc6): @nightly -> 0.2.51-nightly.20260924-003723.ae32250, would upgrade False."
  not_reached: "bob@100.64.0.55: ssh ports 22 and 1004 timed out and ping lost 100% again (2026-09-28 02:4x UTC); not installed."
  cindy_ai_clean_reinstall: "User, 2026-09-28: 'cindy 설치해'. No ciel-runtime process was running (17:01 UTC); 95c5cc6 reinstalled with the normal (non-FORCE) script; import check and `ciel-runtime tokens --help` OK."
  on_target_tests: "cindy-ai (kernel 7.0.0-31-generic, Python 3.12.3), tests.test_terminal_modal_guard + tests.test_pty_master_writer against the installed code: 10 OK, 1 FAIL. The relay test showed no 'exit: No', GOT:[walkie] hello and HELD=True, but CHILD_EXIT=1 instead of 0."
  found_exit_status_race: "Relay log for that run: channel_stdin_proxy_io_failed stage=master_read errno=5 child_running=true exit_status=1. Probe (plain child that reads one line and exits 0, 5 runs each): 95c5cc6 returned 1 in 3/5 and ae32250 in 2/5, while the child's real returncode (reaped after the relay returned) was 0 every time. The master read gets EIO before the child can be reaped, and resolve_posix_child_exit_status (since 0b3daa2, 2026-08-28) reports 1 when proc.poll() is still None. Not changed (no instruction yet). Not verified: whether this return value reaches the 'Claude Code exited with code N' diagnostic in a real launch."
